A||||3||Seanh||Removing the Fuel Rail/Injectors||||5||
Z||000000||Seanh||10-20-2000||09:24 PM||||I have the upper plenum off and removed the cold start line, 2 fuel lines, 2 retaining bolts, and the electrical connectors to the injectors. I cant seem to get the rail and injector assembly to come out. I was affraid to pull to hard on it for fear of damaging the injectors. Do I just need to pull harder? Is there some secret to getting them out? Also, how could I go about cleaning the injectors once I get them out? Thanks<P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8<BR>Killer Stereo System||||reg||5
Z||000001||StuGood||10-20-2000||09:39 PM||||Yep.  You got it.  You just have to pull harder. <P>Just make sure everything's off the fuel rail(FWIW, my less-than-perfect memory tells me that the items you listed, are all there is).<BR>I believe I used a big screwdriver under the fuel rail to get it to come out. Use a piece of wood to protect the aluminum from the tip of the screwdriver.<P>Do it gently; gradually apply more force until it moves a little.  Then pry at a new location.  Keep working on it, prying it up <B>evenly</B>, a little at a time.<P>The injectors come out with the rail- they are installed with o-rings on them, so they will offer some resistance to coming out.<BR>It takes a little guts  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">!<P>Just go slow, be patient, don't break anything, and you'll get it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">! ||||reg||6
Z||000002||Seanh||10-20-2000||10:07 PM||||Okay, Thanks, I just went out and tried again and they came out okay. I am still wonding about cleaning them now if I can. Thanks<P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8<BR>Killer Stereo System||||reg||1
Z||000003||terryk||10-20-2000||11:39 PM||||Use Vaseline on the o-rings to get the injectors back into the intake. One side, then the other.||||reg||1
